# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH at its experimental equilibrium bond
# length (r_e = 1.5949 Angstrom, NIST CCCBDB), 6-31G basis (downloaded
# from https://www.basissetexchange.org/, lih-6-31g.gbs) -- the 4-
# component (C4_SPINOR) counterpart of lih_X2C_gnof_debug.inp, run
# alongside NON_REL in the same file. Evaluates GNOF with TWO
# independent PNOF coupling subspaces (PNOF_SUBSPACES 2): subspace 1
# couples HOMO with LUMO, subspace 2 (a DISJOINT block of orbitals --
# see Input.h's own pnof_subspaces()/pnof_coupling() header comments)
# couples HOMO-1 with LUMO+1, PNOF_COUPLING 2 each (plain pairing, one
# occupied pair to one unoccupied pair per subspace). LiH's 4 electrons
# = exactly 2 occupied pairs (Li 1s core + the Li-H bonding pair), so
# BOTH become frontier (active) geminals here -- no frozen core --
# specifically to exercise Hessian_opt/PnofFock.h's generalized Fock/
# gradient and the e^kappa orbital-rotation finite-difference check
# (main.cpp's buildPnofFunctionalReport, DEBUG TRUE below) with MORE
# THAN ONE active electron pair/geminal-pair coupling, for the
# relativistic 4-component (C4_DHF) path specifically -- see
# lih_X2C_gnof_debug.inp's own header comment for the analogous X2C
# test and the Kramers-phase-convention background this exercises.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
